{"edits": [{"finding_ids": ["app/models.py:17:root-validator", "app/models.py:23:config-class"], "search": "from pydantic import BaseModel, root_validator", "replace": "from pydantic import BaseModel, ConfigDict, model_validator", "explanation": "Imports updated: root_validator is no longer used after the migration. ConfigDict is needed for model_config, and model_validator is needed for the replacement validator (migration guide: @root_validator is deprecated in favor of @model_validator)."}, {"finding_ids": ["app/models.py:17:root-validator"], "search": "    @root_validator
    def compute_total(cls, values):
        lines = values.get("lines") or []
        values["total"] = round(sum(l.qty * l.price for l in lines), 2)
        return values", "replace": "    @model_validator(mode="after")
    def compute_total(self):
        lines = self.lines or []
        self.__dict__["total"] = round(sum(l.qty * l.price for l in lines), 2)
        return self", "explanation": "Per the migration guide, @root_validator should be replaced by @model_validator. In v2 the 'after' mode receives the model instance (an instance method returning self) instead of a values dict, so the body reads self.lines and returns self. The total is written via self.__dict__ rather than self.total = ... because validate_assignment=True is set on this model; a normal attribute assignment inside an after validator would re-trigger model validation on assignment and can recurse. Writing __dict__ keeps the same stored result without that re-entry."}, {"finding_ids": ["app/models.py:23:config-class"], "search": "    class Config:
        validate_assignment = True", "replace": "    model_config = ConfigDict(validate_assignment=True)", "explanation": "Per the 'Changes to config' section of the migration guide, the v1 inner class Config is deprecated; v2 uses a model_config class attribute. The key validate_assignment is unchanged, so the value is preserved."}], "notes": "Two findings addressed (root-validator and config-class) with three edits, including one import edit shared by both. Design choice to flag for review: the root validator is now mode='after' and writes the computed total with self.__dict__["total"] instead of self.total. This is deliberate because validate_assignment=True is set on Order; a plain attribute assignment in an after validator would re-trigger validation and can recurse. If the team prefers plain assignment, verify that it does not recurse in the target pydantic 2.x version. Only models.py was edited; app/service.py is outside this request. The List import is still used by Order.lines, so it stays."}
